{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find the element that appears only once in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    \n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        \n        # If mid is even and arr[mid] == arr[mid+1], or mid is odd and arr[mid] == arr[mid-1]\n        # then the single element is in the right half\n        if (mid % 2 == 0 and mid + 1 < len(arr) and arr[mid] == arr[mid + 1]) or \\\n           (mid % 2 == 1 and arr[mid] == arr[mid - 1]):\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid\n    \n    return arr[left]"}
