{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Count sequences where each element >= 2*previous and <= m.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    dp = {}\n    \n    def count_sequences(length, last_element):\n        if length == 0:\n            return 1\n        if (length, last_element) in dp:\n            return dp[(length, last_element)]\n        \n        total = 0\n        min_next = 2 * last_element if last_element > 0 else 1\n        for next_val in range(min_next, m + 1):\n            total += count_sequences(length - 1, next_val)\n        \n        dp[(length, last_element)] = total\n        return total\n    \n    return count_sequences(n, 0)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Count sequences where each element >= 2*previous and <= m.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of sequences of length i ending with value j\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base case: sequences of length 1\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][j] = 1\n    \n    # Fill dp table\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            # Previous element must be at most j//2\n            for prev in range(1, j // 2 + 1):\n                dp[i][j] += dp[i-1][prev]\n    \n    # Sum all sequences of length n\n    return sum(dp[n][j] for j in range(1, m + 1))"}
