{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, n, k):\n    # Handle edge cases\n    if n == 0 or k == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Find max subarray sum in single array using Kadane's algorithm\n    def kadane(array):\n        max_ending_here = max_so_far = array[0]\n        for i in range(1, len(array)):\n            max_ending_here = max(array[i], max_ending_here + array[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n        return max_so_far\n    \n    # If k = 1, return kadane's result\n    if k == 1:\n        return kadane(arr)\n    \n    # Create array of size 2*n to handle wraparound cases\n    extended_arr = arr + arr\n    max_kadane = kadane(extended_arr)\n    \n    # Calculate prefix and suffix sums\n    prefix_sum = [0] * n\n    suffix_sum = [0] * n\n    \n    prefix_sum[0] = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        prefix_sum[i] = prefix_sum[i-1] + arr[i]\n    \n    suffix_sum[n-1] = arr[n-1]\n    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):\n        suffix_sum[i] = suffix_sum[i+1] + arr[i]\n    \n    max_prefix = max(prefix_sum)\n    max_suffix = max(suffix_sum)\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n    \n    # Result is maximum of three cases\n    result = max_kadane\n    \n    # If total sum is positive and k > 2, we can benefit from middle arrays\n    if total_sum > 0 and k > 2:\n        result = max(result, max_prefix + max_suffix + (k-2) * total_sum)\n    else:\n        result = max(result, max_prefix + max_suffix)\n    \n    return result"}
