{"task_id": "Mbpp/590", "solution": "def polar_rect(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Convert polar coordinates to rectangular coordinates.\"\"\"\n    import math\n    r = math.sqrt(a**2 + b**2)\n    theta = math.atan2(b, a)\n    x = r * math.cos(theta)\n    y = r * math.sin(theta)\n    return ((r, theta), complex(x, y))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/590", "solution": "def polar_rect(r, theta):\n    import math\n    import cmath\n    \n    # Convert to rectangular coordinates\n    x = r * math.cos(theta)\n    y = r * math.sin(theta)\n    \n    # Calculate magnitude and phase\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(x*x + y*y)\n    phase = math.atan2(y, x)\n    \n    # Return as tuple of (magnitude, phase) and complex number\n    return ((magnitude, phase), complex(x, y))"}
